NAME
    command - run a command without alias expansion, or check existence

SYNOPSIS
    command <name> [args...]
    command -v <name>...

DESCRIPTION
    With no options, runs <name> with [args...] while bypassing shell
    aliases. For example, 'command quit' fails as an unknown command even
    though 'quit' is an alias for shutdown(1). Built-in language commands
    still resolve to themselves.

    With -v, prints each <name> that resolves to a builtin, alias, or
    command, one per line, and prints nothing for names that do not
    resolve.

OPTIONS
    -v  Print resolvable command names instead of executing them.

EXAMPLES
    command echo hello
    if command -v grep; then echo found; fi

EXIT STATUS
    0   In execution mode, the invoked command's exit status (0 on
        success). With -v, every named command was found.
    1   Unknown command, invalid usage, or with -v at least one name was
        not found.

SEE ALSO
    which(1), help(1), dianash(1)
